  "title": "Adapting to the impacts of heatwaves in a changing climate in Botkyrka, Sweden",
  "summary": "Botkyrka responded to increased heatwaves by Climatools program project, creating checklists for homes and schools during heatwaves, enhancing warning systems, distributing targeted information, and establishing 'cool spots' for public use, effectively mitigating health risks during extreme heat. In the last century, heatwaves in Sweden occurred once every 20 years (the last being in 1975). Since the start of the new millennium, four heatwaves (2003, 2007, 2010 and 2018) have been already experienced. The frequency of these events is expected to further increase due to climate change; they will occur once every three to five years towards the end of the century.",
